  <h2 id="seat">What your BSc Agriculture seat really is</h2>

  <p>
    Before you compare careers, check the seat behind your degree. The degree is a four-year BSc (Hons) in most universities, and ICAR now treats all agriculture degrees as professional degrees. Entry runs through one national exam and several other routes.
  </p>

  <p>
    One rule surprises many families: the national exam asks for any three of Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics, Biology and Agriculture in Class 12. So a PCM student can apply, and Biology is not compulsory. Each university can still add its own subject list, so read the annexure for the one you want.
  </p>

