    The seat count is for 2025-26, printed in the 2026 bulletin as a guide. The 2026-27 number comes in the counselling brochure. The ICAR list also names BSc (Hons) Natural Farming and BSc (Hons) Agribusiness Management as separate four-year degrees, so a few of the routes below have their own degree too.
  </p>

  <h2 id="routes">Twelve BSc Agriculture career options, ordered by growth room</h2>

  <p>
    The first route sells a skill you can repeat for many farms, so it leads. The business routes follow, because each has a real customer and something you can own. The three exam doors sit last: a hard entry test, then a separate climb later. "Scalable" means your income and reach can keep growing through skills, consulting or a business of your own.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--routes">
