          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="script-box">
    <p class="script-box__label">A first message to an FPO head or input dealer</p>
    <p>
      "I studied BSc Agriculture. I wrote a one-page crop plan for my uncle's two-acre plot of groundnut and kept a photo log. Could I spend a morning at your meeting or counter, and share a short note on what I saw? I will not take more of your time than that."
    </p>
    <p>
      It names one piece of proof and asks one small thing. One number to watch for any route: enquiries that turn into a second visit or a paid job.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Work style matters too. Advice, data and FPO planning can be done partly from a small town or remotely. Farm, shop and drone work need you on site, so choose with your daily life in mind. English helps with company jobs and reading notices, and your home language wins farmers.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">Drones, apps and AI in farm work</h2>

  <p>
    Government schemes now push drones and apps toward farms. For a graduate, the question is which of your tasks they take and which they create.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Task</th>
          <th>Pressure from AI or drones</th>
          <th>What stays with a person</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
